<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14042" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dīnŭmĕrātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				counting over, reckoning up, enumeration</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen. (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">noctium ac dierum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Rep. 3, 2 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(dierum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Paul. Sent. 5, 33</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(personarum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 38, 10, 10, § 16</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. 2 Par. 2,
			17</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Esp., as a figure of speech, i. q. Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαρίθμησις</span>, <i><span class="en">Cic. de
				Or. 3, 54, 207</span></i>; quoted ap. <i><span class="en">Quint. 9,
				1, 35</span></i> (who, however, does not regard it as a figure); 9,
			3, 91 Spald.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
